  "question": {
    "text": "A hydrogen atom changes its state from $n=3$ to $n=2$. Due to recoil, the percentage change in the wave length of emitted light is approximately $1 \\times 10^{-n}$. The value of $n$ is_____. \n[Given $\\mathrm{Rhc}=13.6 \\mathrm{eV}, \\mathrm{hc}=1242 \\mathrm{eV} \\mathrm{nm}, \\mathrm{h}=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~s}$ mass of the hydrogenatom $=1.6 \\times 10^{-27} \\mathrm{~kg}$ ]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{E}=13.6\\left(\\frac{1}{2^2}-\\frac{1}{3^2}\\right)=1.9 \\mathrm{eV} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda} \\\\\n& \\lambda=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\Delta \\mathrm{E}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{i}}=\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{t}} \\\\\n& 0=-\\mathrm{mv}+\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\lambda^{\\prime \\prime}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{v}=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{m} \\lambda^{\\prime}} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{mv^{2 }}+\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda^{\\prime \\prime}} \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{m} \\lambda^{\\prime}}\\right)^2+\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda^{\\prime}}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Now\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{h^2}{2 \\mathrm{~m} \\lambda^{\\prime^2}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda^{\\prime}} \\\\\n& \\lambda^{\\prime 2} \\Delta \\mathrm{E}-\\mathrm{hc} \\lambda^{\\prime}-\\frac{\\mathrm{h}^2}{2 \\mathrm{~m}}=0 \\\\\n& \\lambda^{\\prime}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc} \\pm \\sqrt{\\mathrm{h}^2 \\mathrm{c}^2+\\frac{4 \\Delta \\mathrm{Eh}^2}{2 \\mathrm{~m}}}}{2 \\Delta \\mathrm{E}} \\\\\n& \\lambda^{\\prime}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc} \\pm \\mathrm{hc} \\sqrt{1+\\frac{2 \\Delta \\mathrm{E}}{\\mathrm{mc}}}}{2 \\Delta \\mathrm{E}}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\lambda^{\\prime}}{\\lambda}=\\frac{1+\\left(1+\\frac{2 \\Delta \\mathrm{E}}{\\mathrm{mc}^2}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{2}=\\frac{1+1+\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{E}}{\\mathrm{mc}^2}}{2} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\lambda^{\\prime}}{\\lambda}=1+\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{E}}{2 \\mathrm{mc}^2} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\lambda^{\\prime}-\\lambda}{\\lambda}=\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{E}}{2 \\mathrm{mc}^2}=\\frac{1.9 \\times 1.6 \\times 10^{-19}}{2 \\times 1.67 \\times 10^{-27} \\times 9 \\times 10^{15}}=10^{-9} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\% \\text { change } \\approx 10^{-7}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Correct answer 7",
    "image": null
  },
